  "body": "Follow-up from #794 (TTS holders in the built-in holder library). Labels to set at triage: P2, effort:high, area:sim, source:agent (the filer, a fork agent, could not set labels).\n\n**What:** a machine file (`.mch`) has no notion of a spindle mount or default holder, so new tools cannot default to a library holder per machine. #794 was asked to \"let the 770MX machine file default new tools to TTS where the holder model supports a machine default\" - it does not, so this is filed instead of built.\n\n**Correction to #794's premise, from Tormach's public pages:** the **770MX and 1100MX have a BT30 spindle**, not TTS (https://www.tormach.com/tormach_mills/ - \"MX machines have a BT30 spindle\"; \"PCNC and M machines have an R8 collet in the spindle and use TTS tool holders\"). So the defaults should be:\n- `tormach-770mx`, `tormach-770mx-ml`, `tormach-1100mx`, `tormach-1500mx`: a BT30 holder (e.g. \"BT30 ER20\");\n- `tormach-770m`, `tormach-770m-plus`, `tormach-1100m`, `tormach-1100m-plus`, `tormach-pcnc770*`, `tormach-pcnc1100-*`, `tormach-pcnc440`: TTS (e.g. \"TTS ER20\").\n\n**Shape (proposal):** an optional `tooling.default_holder` string in the machine file naming a `holder_library` entry, validated at load (unknown name refused by name); `AddTool` (GUI and MCP) applies it through `SetToolBody::library` in the same undo step when the active machine names one; an existing tool is never changed.\n\n**Done means:** the field parses and validates; the Tormach machine files carry it; a new tool on the 770MX lands with \"BT30 ER20\" and on the 770M with \"TTS ER20\" (pinned by an app test, one undo removes tool and holder together); an unknown holder name in a machine file is a named load error.\n\nPart of #743. Related: #794, #799 (MCP holder tool).\n",
